.TH MICROVM-MCP 1 "September 2026" "microvm-mcp" "Administrator Commands"
.SH NAME
microvm-mcp \- private development microVM service and administrator CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B microvm-mcp serve --config
.I FILE
.br
.B microvm-mcp issue-token --state-dir
.I DIRECTORY
.B --workspace
.I NAME
.B --output
.I FILE
.RB [ --image
.IR ID ]...
.br
.B microvm-mcp revoke-workspace --state-dir
.I DIRECTORY
.B --workspace
.I NAME
.br
.B microvm-mcp demo-manifest --endpoint
.I URL
.br
.B microvm-mcp attach --token-file
.I FILE
.B --vm
.I VM_ID
.B --port
.I PORT
.RB [ --endpoint
.IR URL ]
.RB [ --ignore-stdin-eof ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs workspace-authorized Firecracker microVMs over HTTP and MCP.
The serve command requires root, KVM, cgroup v2, pinned guest artifacts and
reflink-capable storage. Configure the service before enabling its systemd unit.
Use each subcommand's --help option for its complete arguments.
.PP
Workspace credentials are issued locally and written to mode-0600 files.
Never place credentials in guest images, model prompts or tool arguments.
Workspace revocation denies future requests and closes open guest streams,
but does not stop existing jobs. issue-token --image restricts a workspace to
the named guest images.
.PP
The attach command bridges standard input and output to a vsock port of an
owned VM, for example as an MCP client's stdio server command. It reads the
credential from a file. Firecracker has no vsock half-close: after standard
input ends, the guest reads EOF but cannot reply.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/microvm-mcp.toml
.br
.I /var/lib/microvm-mcp
.br
.I /usr/share/doc/microvm-mcp/README.Debian
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR microvm-mcp-install-image (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
